Report a read error from the whois server.
A read error, such as a connection reset by the server, ended the
reply as if the server had closed the connection normally, so whois
showed a truncated reply, or followed or skipped a redirect based on
it, and exited with status 0. Check the stream's error indicator and
die with "read error".

---
 networking/whois.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/networking/whois.c
+++ b/networking/whois.c
@@ -97,6 +97,8 @@
 			}
 		}
 	}
+	if (ferror(fp))
+		bb_simple_perror_msg_and_die(bb_msg_read_error);
 	if (midline) {
 		/* end the last line */
 		buf = xrealloc(buf, bufpos + 2);
